 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Thresholds (CI Gating)
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object to gate CI on metric scores (e.g. `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`).
+- Thresholds are reported in both JSON (`passed` field + `thresholds` array) and Markdown formats.
+- A metric with no score (e.g., exact match without references) fails its threshold instead of crashing or passing.
+- CLI exposes `--threshold metric=<min>` flags (repeatable); validates format and values at parse time; exits 1 if any fail, 2 if malformed.
+- Without `--threshold`, report and exit code behave as before (no `passed`/`thresholds` fields).
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
